# Template for a new song. Copy to <slug>.song, drop the .example suffix,
# and add it to ../order.txt.
#
# Metadata is absolute: the key written here is the key played. There is no
# separate transposition for the grid and the lyrics.
title:  Song Title
artist: Artist
key:    Gm
tempo:  96
time:   4/4
# capo:   2          # annotates only; it does not transpose
# flats:  yes        # force flat spelling; omitted uses the conventional table

# Sections are [Label]. A grid is bars between | separators:
#   | Gm |              one chord, the whole bar
#   | Gm . . Cm |       beat grid: Gm for three beats, Cm on four
#   |: Gm | Bb :|       repeat
#   | (1.) Gm |         first-time ending
#   | % |               play the previous bar again
#   | %% |              play the previous two bars
# Four bars per system is the default; `bars: 6` overrides for a 6-bar phrase.
#
# Lyric lines carry chords inline: Some [Gm]words here

[Intro]
grid: |: Gm | Bb | Dm | C :|

[Verse]
grid: | Gm | Bb | F | C |
Lyrics go here, with [Gm]chords over the syllable they start on

[Chorus]
grid: | Eb . . F | Gm |
